The problem is in the termcap driver, near as I can tell.  I'm using
an old termcap I had from 2.3 and it doesn't show this problem. (I've set
term=ansi-mono which gives a nice black background but still has all the colors
and looks the nicest I've seen.  Because this is an annoying problem, I'll
type in my termcap entries:
#
ansi-mono:\
        :co#80:\
        :li#24:\
        :cl=\E[2J:\
        :bs:\
        :ho=\E[H:\
        :cm=\E[%i%2;%2H:\
        :up=\E[A:\
        :xd=\E[B:\
        :nd=\E[C:\
        :bc=\E[D:\
        :ce=\E[K:\
        :ti=\E[m:\
        :te=\E[m:\
        :so=\E[1m:\
        :se=\E[m:\
        :us=\E[1m:\
        :ue=\E[m:\

Heee! I'm so happy. I just pasted that in from the Microsoft Windows notepad
to the QVT VT100 emulator and save me having to type it.
I don't know what the diferences are, but there's lots of them and they
are signifcant.
